             "tag": "div",
             "data": {
              "content": "Etymology-content"
             },
             "content": "Inherited from Ottoman Turkish اوقومق (okumak, “to read, decipher, study, learn, recite, chant, sing”), from Old Anatolian Turkish اوقمق (oqımaq, “to read”), from Proto-Turkic *okï- (“to call, read, recite”).\nCognate with Old Turkic [script needed] (okı-, “to read, call”), Azerbaijani oxumaq (“to read, sing”), Bashkir уҡыу (uqıw, “to read”), Kazakh оқу (oquw, “to read, recite”), Kyrgyz окуу (okuu, “to read, study”), Turkmen okamak (“to read, study”), Uzbek oʻqimoq (“to learn, study, read”), Yakut угуй (uguy, “to call”)."
            }
